**Proposition 4.3 (a concrete source certificate).** At
$Z=1/2$, $c=1/4$, $k=1/8$, $a=1/16$, the four states in (QC.23) have
Gram matrix

$$
G=\begin{pmatrix}
1&0&1/2&1/2\\
0&1&1/2&1/2\\
1/2&1/2&1&0\\
1/2&1/2&0&1
\end{pmatrix},
\qquad \operatorname{rank}G=3.
\tag{QC.34}
$$

Their four rectangle coefficients (QC.24) are $0,8\pi,0,8\pi$,
respectively. The common support margin is $1/16$, and the common
canonical preparation's live probability is $1/3$.

Proof. Here $4k-2c=0$ and $2Z-1=0$, giving (QC.34) directly.
Its leading three-by-three minor has determinant $1/2$; its rows satisfy
$G_1+G_2=G_3+G_4$, so its rank is exactly three. Substitution in
(QC.24) gives $B_{\beta,m}=8\beta-4\pi m$ and the listed coefficients.
The minimum in (QC.26) is $1/16$. The probability descent from $1/8$ to
$1/16$ contributes survival $2/3$, the return contributes $1/2$, and all
constant-height legs contribute one under (QC.7). Their product is $1/3$.
These are the supplier's survival factors used as reachability evidence;
no new survival optimum is claimed. $\square$

